/-!
# Two more eventual words excluded from the centre column of rule 30

For the single-seed evolution of rule 30, the centre column is never eventually the repeating word
`0000000001` (one black cell and nine white cells, `1 0^9` up to phase) nor the word `00000001011`,
whatever the transient. Each proof is a rank certificate in the format of the kit's
`Rule30StripCertificates`, checked by the Lean kernel with `decide +kernel`; the soundness theorem
`Cert.not_eventuallyWord` is the kit's.
Research and formalization by OpenAI Codex for @AIOvernight.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option Elab.async false
set_option maxRecDepth 1000000
set_option maxHeartbeats 0

namespace Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30Certificates.WordExclusions
open Ruliology.CellularAutomata.Rule30StripCertificates

